                <pb facs="0653" n="533" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg533"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Powell to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Amreican Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March 21,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Powell reports that Syrians, naturalized citizens of the United States, are
                    not included in the order of expulsion; that he has instructed American citizens
                    to close their stores on April 1 in order to prevent danger from the populace,
                    who may pillage and set fire to the houses of our citizens. All quiet at the
                    present moment.)</p>
            </div>
